 + session_start Handler", "members": ["chunk2-jiti-module-cache", "chunk2-panel-extension", "chunk2-session-start-handler"], "rationale": "Together, these three concepts created the persistent bug: the panel extension auto-showed on session_start via overlay, and jiti cache served stale compiled files even after source fixes \u00e2\u20ac\u201d making the bug invisible to debugging.", "source_file": "DASHBOARD_POSTMORTEM.md"}, {"id": "hyperedge-chunk2-orchestrator-reliability-chain", "label": "Orchestrator Reliability Chain: OI-1 Verifier Trust + OI-2 Large Tasks + OI-4 Intake Override", "members": ["chunk2-verifier-text-only-trust", "chunk2-executor-task-size-problem", "chunk2-intake-normalizer-override"], "rationale": "OI-1, OI-2, and OI-4 form an interconnected reliability failure chain: large tasks (OI-2) cause executors to write reports not code, the verifier trusts those reports (OI-1), and intake overrides user model preferences (OI-4) \u00e2\u20ac\u201d together enabling undetected implementation failures.", "source_file": "DASHBOARD_POSTMORTEM.md"}, {"id": "hyperedge-chunk2-dashboard-architecture-pattern", "label": "Dashboard Architecture Pattern: Inline Handler + try/catch/finally + setWidget", "members": ["chunk2-suggested-architecture", "chunk2-orchestrate-command-handler", "chunk2-ctx-ui-setwidget-api", "chunk2-finally-block-cleanup"], "rationale": "The recommended dashboard architecture: inline helper functions within the /orchestrate command handler, using setWidget API in a try/catch/finally pattern guaranteeing cleanup.", "source_file": "DASHBOARD_POSTMORTEM.md"}]}